This commit introduces a new `#[swift_bridge(Sendable)]`
attribute that emits Swift `Sendable` implementations for opaque
Rust types, and Rust `Send + Sync` implementations for opaque
Swift types.

These implementations are checked at compile time.

Example usage:
```rust
mod ffi {
    extern "Rust" {
        #[swift_bridge(Sendable)]
        type MyRustType;
    }

    extern "Swift" {
        #[swift_bridge(Sendable)]
        type MySwiftType;
    }
}
```

This PR merges AIFoundryClient logic into the existing **CloudMachineClient**. It also introduces a new **AIFoundryFeature**, which allows a Foundry connection to be added to the `CloudMachineInfrastructure`. In the short term, this feature transfers Foundry connections into the `CloudMachineClient` without provisioning. Long term, it can be extended to generate Bicep/ARM templates for Foundry resources.

**Impact:**
- Existing CloudMachine scenarios continue to work as before.
- Users can now add a Foundry project to their CloudMachine setup by adding `new AIFoundryFeature(connectionString)` to their `CloudMachineInfrastructure`.
- Future improvements can expand AIFoundryFeature to provision Foundry resources alongside other CloudMachine features.

**Example:**
```csharp
 CloudMachineInfrastructure infrastrucutre= new();
 infrastrucutre.AddFeature(new OpenAIModelFeature("gpt-4o-mini", "2024-07-18"));

 var connectionString = TestEnvironment.AzureAICONNECTIONSTRING;
 infrastrucutre.AddFeature(new AIFoundryFeature(connectionString));

 if (infrastrucutre.TryExecuteCommand(args)) return;

 CloudMachineClient client = infrastrucutre.GetClient();
 AgentsClient agents = client.GetAgentsClient();
```

